<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-05-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain</p>
<p>have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to</p>
<p>the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Auk		  unloading   sunflower meal  5,400</p>
<p>				     bran wheat	5,008</p>
<p>Liberty Sun	20/5	  wheat	    53,650     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	   8,190</p>
<p>Belle		21/5	  soya	     22,600     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	   5,100</p>
<p>				     corn screening  7,000</p>
<p>Mediz		21/5	  sunflower seeds 2,919     Europe</p>
<p>Volgobal196	23/5     wheat	     2,800	  Europe</p>
<p>Ocean Lane 2     24/5	  rapeseed meal   7,500     Europe</p>
<p>Athos		25/5	  fish meal	 1,260     Peru</p>
<p>Europa	     26/5	  corn	     20,500     U.S.</p>
<p>				     barley	   19,870</p>
<p>				     sunflower meal  3,600</p>
<p>Gencis K.	  02/6	  gluten feed     8,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     gluten meal     3,800</p>
<p>				     sorgum	    8,000</p>
<p>				     soya	     17,000</p>
<p>				     corn screening  6,000</p>
<p>				     wheat	     2,000</p>
<p>Fany		 05/6	  corn+wheat     35,000     U.S.</p>
<p>First Lady	 10/6	  soya+sorghum   25,000     U.S.</p>
<p>					+wheat</p>
<p>TBN		  14/6	  barley	   22,650     U.S.</p>
